course: dictionary
lesson: 8889
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To know which meaning is meant, read the context: the words and sentences around it. «The shrew scurried under the hedge, looking for worms.» Scurrying and hunting for worms show that a shrew is an animal here.
explain: «She turned into a shrew when her brother broke her model.» This is a different meaning. A shrew here is a bad-tempered woman who scolds. The clues are the anger and the scolding, and the dictionary tells us this old use is insulting.
explain: Check your choice by putting the meaning back into the sentence. If the animal meaning makes no sense, try the other one. Good readers test their clues before they decide.
fact: A shrew is a tiny mammal with a long pointed nose, small eyes and soft fur.
fact: A shrew looks a bit like a mouse, but it eats insects and worms.
fact: «Shrews are tiny fierce hunters of insects and worms.» They must eat almost all the time because they burn energy very fast.
fact: Owls and cats hunt shrews, so shrews are food for other animals.
fact: Long ago, shrew also meant a bad-tempered woman who often scolds; this use is now seen as unkind.
exercise: «Shrews are tiny fierce hunters of insects and worms.» What is a shrew in this sentence? | A bad-tempered woman who scolds | *A tiny animal that hunts insects and worms | A large bird that lives in trees | A soft kind of cloth
exercise: «She turned into a shrew when her brother broke her model.» What does shrew mean here? | A small dog that barks | *A bad-tempered woman who scolds | A tiny mammal with a long pointed nose | A kind and gentle teacher
exercise: Why do shrews have to eat almost all the time? | Because they cannot find any water | Because they like sweet things best | Because they sleep during the day only | *Because they burn energy very fast
test: Shrews look a bit like which animal? | A fish | *A mouse | A frog | A horse
test: What is the old, insulting meaning of shrew? | A petrol station | A dark cave under a hill | A tiny mammal that eats worms | *A bad-tempered woman who often scolds
exam: «The shrew was hunting beetles under the leaves.» Which meaning fits? | A kind of tall tree | *The tiny animal that hunts insects | A loud musical instrument | The old insult for a scolding woman
